<h1>Debug feedback</h1>

<p class="lede">
    Reports what a page actually did: the element you picked, the CSS
    rules that matched it, the browser it happened in, and whatever
    failed to load along the way.
</p>

<h2>Install the bookmarklet</h2>

<p>
    Drag this to your bookmarks toolbar, or right-click it and choose
    <em>Bookmark link</em>. Pasting a <code>javascript:</code> URL into
    the address bar will not work — both browsers strip it.
</p>

<p><a class="bookmarklet" href="#">Debug feedback</a></p>

<details>
    <summary>Or copy the URL by hand</summary>
    <pre class="bookmarklet-source"></pre>
</details>

<h2>Using it</h2>

<dl>
    <dt>Pick an element</dt>
    <dd>
        Choose what kind of problem it is, then click the element. The
        arrow keys walk the tree — <kbd>↑</kbd> to the parent,
        <kbd>↓</kbd> to the first child, <kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd>
        between siblings — because the element worth reporting is usually
        the container, not the leaf the mouse can reach.
        <kbd>Enter</kbd> locks it, <kbd>Esc</kbd> cancels.
    </dd>

    <dt>Choose what to send</dt>
    <dd>
        Each channel is a switch with its own size, and
        <em>Show exactly what will be sent</em> renders the payload
        before it goes. Form values, password fields and anything marked
        <code>data-debug-feedback-redact</code> never leave the page.
    </dd>

    <dt>Screenshots</dt>
    <dd>
        Optional, and captured by the browser's own screen-capture
        permission so the image shows your real rendering. Share
        <strong>this tab</strong> rather than a window or a screen:
        cropping and the black bars over form fields only work when the
        frame can be mapped to the page, and the widget will say so if it
        cannot.
    </dd>
</dl>

<h2>Where it works</h2>

<% if sites.nil? %>
    <p>No allowlist configured: reports are accepted from any site.</p>
<% else %>
    <p>Reports are accepted from these hosts only:</p>
    <ul>
        <% sites.each do |site| %>
            <li><code><%= site %></code></li>
        <% end %>
    </ul>
<% end %>

<p>
    The bookmarklet loads on any page, but a report is posted to
    <code>/.debug-feedback/report/</code> on <em>that page's own host</em>.
    On a site without the endpoint mounted it will fail at the moment you
    press send, with the report already written. Mounting it elsewhere is
    one line in that vhost's config.
</p>

<h2>State</h2>

<dl class="state">
    <dt>Reports</dt>
    <dd><a href="review/"><%= count %> stored</a></dd>

    <dt>Latest</dt>
    <dd><%= latest ? "#{latest["at"]} — #{latest["url"]}" : "none yet" %></dd>

    <dt>Store</dt>
    <dd><code><%= store_path %></code></dd>

    <dt>Endpoint</dt>
    <dd><a href="report/health">health</a></dd>
</dl>

<script>
    /* The app is behind a proxy and is not told its public URL, but the
       browser knows it: this page is being served from it. */
    (function () {
        var src = location.origin + "/common/js/debug-feedback.js";
        var code = "javascript:(function(){var s=document.createElement('script');" +
                   "s.src='" + src + "';document.body.appendChild(s);})();";
        document.querySelector(".bookmarklet").href = code;
        document.querySelector(".bookmarklet-source").textContent = code;
    })();
</script>
